{"_id":"6a2ff4d72204ffbc59e5a596","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"PlFcaQsvFSK0Y-LKGu0eH","description":"# Indexing & Slicing\n\nPandas provides two primary indexing systems: `.loc[]` for label-based selection and `.iloc[]` for position-based selection. Both work on rows, columns, or both simultaneously. Boolean indexing with a condition (e.g., `df[df['age'] > 30]`) is the most common way to filter rows.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"pandas.DataFrame.loc","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.DataFrame.loc.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb65"},{"type":"official","title":"pandas.DataFrame.iloc","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.DataFrame.iloc.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb66"},{"type":"article","title":"Iloc vs Loc in Pandas: A Guide with Examples","url":"https://www.analyticsvidhya.com/blog/2026/03/iloc-vs-loc-in-pandas/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb67"},{"type":"video","title":"Pandas loc and iloc","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=naRQyRZrXCE","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb68"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:49:27.695Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/PlFcaQsvFSK0Y-LKGu0eH.md"}